 "primary_comparison_asymmetry_disclosure": {
  "pre_registered_primary_reads": "best_<metric> = MAX over the R refactor rounds",
  "single_shot_reads": "its ONE grade",
  "why_this_matters": "Per-cell change_accuracy is BINARY at these window sizes (exactly one gradeable acceptance row per game), so a refinement arm that changes nothing still scores 1-(1-p)^R against single-shot's p -- 0.36 vs 0.20 at p=0.2, R=2 -- from the extra draw alone, and the max is taken over the same held-out block that grades. `treatment_vs_control` is symmetric and unaffected. The like-for-like final-round contrast is reported above and a POSITIVE verdict requires both.",
